{#- The box: one field for anything a reader wants to say to targum, and the four ways
    out of it. It is one file because it stands on two pages — Learn, where it is the
    front door (2026-09-06, design.md §12), and the conversation page, where it is the
    composer — and two copies of a box drift the way two copies of a nav bar did.

    Left to right, on one row since 2026-09-10 (targum-internal#235): the `+`, which
    holds a file, a picture or a recording in the box for Send to bring (it used to be
    Upload, a corner of the nav; it is a thing you do while asking, not a place, and
    since 2026-09-06 the Add page is its "More options"); the field; Speak, shown only
    where the browser records and the reader has modern Hebrew to speak (the page's
    script decides both); and Send, the working action, in the accent. Speak and Send
    are glyphs from `_glyphs.html.j2` with the word as their label — the notes of
    2026-09-10: "default to icons in lieu of text" — and the `+` stays typed (§7).

    Set `placeholder` before including. Every id here is what `chat.js` and `box.js`
    look for. -#}
{% include '_glyphs.html.j2' %}
<form class="composer" id="composer">
  {#- One row from the start: the field grows with what is typed, to six lines or so,
      and then scrolls. `rows="1"` is the resting height; the stylesheet does the rest. -#}
  <textarea id="say" rows="1" placeholder="{{ placeholder }}" spellcheck="true"
            aria-label="Your message"></textarea>
  {#- A file, a recording or a book, chosen here and priced in place: the Add page's
      job in one press, since 2026-09-06. A link goes in the field like anything else
      said to targum. The card it draws carries "More options", which is the Add page,
      for a translation or a transcript of your own. -#}
  <button type="button" class="chat-bring" id="chat-bring"
          aria-label="Bring a file, a picture or a recording"
          title="Bring a file, a picture or a recording">+</button>
  {#- `multiple` for the pictures: several chosen together are the pages of one text
      (2026-09-07). Anything else is taken one at a time, whatever was selected. -#}
  <input type="file" id="chat-file" hidden multiple
         accept=".txt,.md,.markdown,.epub,.pdf,.png,.jpg,.jpeg,.webp,.heic,.heif,.mp3,.m4a,.m4b,.aac,.ogg,.opus,.flac,.wav,.mp4,.m4v,.mov,.webm,.mkv">
  {#- What the + chose, held in the box until Send (2026-09-07): a chip a file, each
      with a way to let it go. Choosing is not yet bringing; Send is, the way it is for
      a line — the card is then a turn in the conversation, never a thing under the box. -#}
  <ul class="chat-held" id="chat-held" hidden></ul>
  {#- Push-to-talk, and called that: a clip goes up, is written down, and comes back
      as a line — seconds, not a conversation. -#}
  <button type="button" class="chat-mic" id="chat-mic" aria-pressed="false" hidden
          aria-label="Speak" title="Speak"><svg class="glyph" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use class="glyph-use" href="#glyph-mic"/></svg></button>
  <button type="submit" class="chat-send" id="chat-send" aria-label="Send" title="Send"><svg class="glyph" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#glyph-send"/></svg></button>
</form>
{#- What went wrong with a line, said under the box in words (§6), never in colour
    alone. -#}
<p class="chat-said" id="chat-said" role="status" hidden></p>
